<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bartolomeu Dias</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1450–<a href="/years/1500">1500</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bartolomeu Dias was a Portuguese navigator who in 1488 became the first European known to sail around the southern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-of-good-hope">Cape of Good Hope</a>. His voyage proved that the Atlantic connected with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>. It opened the way for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasco-da-gama">Vasco da Gama</a>'s voyage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bartolomeu-dias.jpg" alt="Bartolomeu Dias" width="189" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bartolomeu_Dias,_South_Africa_House.JPG: RedCoat (en:User:RedCoat10) derivative work: Biser Todorov (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bartolomeu_Dias,_South_Africa_House_(cut).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
